# musallahboard-agent — privileged commands allow-list
#
# The agent's command channel can request:
#   - kiosk.restart  → /bin/systemctl restart musallahboard-kiosk.service
#   - system.reboot  → /bin/systemctl reboot
#
# Both invoked as `sudo -n <cmd>` from the agent. We allow only those exact
# argument sets so a compromised agent can bounce the kiosk or reboot, but
# can't, say, install packages or open a root shell.
#
# Install: drop into /etc/sudoers.d/ with mode 0440 owned by root:root.
#
# `musallahdaemon` is a fixed, package-owned system account — it is NOT
# configurable, and must match User= in musallahboard-agent.service. Keeping it
# fixed is what lets this file ship verbatim in a .deb with no substitution.
# It is deliberately a name no human would choose for a login: an earlier
# revision used `admin`, which collided with the human sudo account on Pi
# installs and silently ran the agent with NOPASSWD:ALL.

musallahdaemon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl restart musallahboard-kiosk.service
musallahdaemon ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /bin/systemctl reboot
